1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nf3 { The Perseus Gambit White is sacrificing a pawn for little compensation. White is going to play Ne5 to try and as much as possible to pressurize the f7 pawn and so on. There are a few traps that may arose from this position. } { [%csl Yf3][%cal Yf3e5] } 3... dxe4 4. Ne5 { One of white's goal is to tempt black from playing the move f6?? Which falls into Qf3+! Thus losing g6 is forced and thereby losing material. } (4. Ng5 { Ng6 is another alternative which white once again lures black to play f6?? And of course to take back the pawn } 4... Nf6 { [%csl Rf6][%cal Rf6e4] } 5. Be3 { [%csl Rh7] } 5... h6 6. Nh3 { Simply develop your other knight and your life would have been a lot better either ways. } 6... Nc6 7. Nd2 Be7 8. Bb5 O-O) 4... Nf6 { Black must simply develop and try to hold unto the e pawn before things get a bit uncanny from the starting point of the opening trap. } 5. Be3 (5. Bg5 Nbd7 6. Nd2 Be7 7. c3 h6 8. Be3 O-O) 5... Bd6 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Bg5 h6 8. Bh4 Nbd7 { Black must try to hold on the pawn but of course at the same time simply develop and castle short 0-0 } 9. Bc4 Nxe5 10. dxe5 Qxd1+ 11. Rxd1 Nd5 *


